# SkillBridge AI is a static, client-only site (no server, no bundler at
# runtime). This file is NOT read by the browser — it only documents the one
# environment variable Vercel's build step (scripts/generate-config.js) reads
# to produce config.js, which sets a default AI key for all visitors.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY
#   Optional. Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   Set this in your Vercel project's Environment Variables (Dashboard ->
#   Settings -> Environment Variables), NOT in a committed file.
#
#   WARNING: this app has no backend to keep a key secret. Any value set here
#   ships inside a public JS file (config.js) that every visitor's browser can
#   read (view-source, dev tools, network tab). Only set this if you're fine
#   with that — e.g. a free-tier key with a low quota and, ideally, HTTP
#   referrer restrictions configured in Google AI Studio.
#
#   Leaving it unset is the safe default: the app works fully offline via its
#   built-in Smart AI Engine, and visitors can optionally add their own key
#   through the in-app "⚙️ AI Settings" button — stored only in their own
#   browser's localStorage, never sent anywhere but the AI provider they chose.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_free_gemini_api_key_here
